Are you technically minded and looking for a challenging role in an innovative high-tech environment? Then this position as a VAS Technician could be the perfect opportunity for you!

You will work alongside a team of technicians and specialists, assembling, testing, and configuring advanced equipment. No two days are the same, and you will have plenty of opportunities to further develop your technical skills. In this role, you will be responsible for assembling, installing, and preparing technical equipment according to customer requirements. You will ensure that all products meet the required quality standards before they are shipped or installed.

Your responsibilities include:

- Assembling equipment and network setups according to instructions and customer requirements;
- Unpacking, preparing, and installing technical equipment;
- Performing quality inspections and technical verification activities;
- Identifying and reporting technical issues during assembly, testing, and installation processes;
- Following work instructions accurately and processing documentation correctly;
- Supporting installation, configuration, and disassembly activities;
- Maintaining a safe working environment at all times;
- Collaborating with colleagues and technical specialists to achieve project objectives;
- Participating in training programs to further develop your technical knowledge and skills.

You have a technical background and are motivated to further develop yourself within a high-tech environment. In addition, you recognize yourself in the following:

- You have completed a technical education at a minimum of MBO Level 4 or equivalent;
- You have a good command of the English language, at least B2 level;
- You are eager to learn and have an affinity for technology;
- Experience within a logistics or production environment is an advantage but not required;
- You are flexible and enjoy working as part of a team;
- You are accurate and have a strong eye for quality;
- You

In the role of Quality Control Specialist, you will take charge of preserving product quality at every step of the production cycle. Your key responsibilities involve:
- Carrying out precise measurements and sampling in line with predefined standards;
- Reviewing and authorizing product batches prior to their transfer to storage;
- Overseeing and ensuring quality consistency throughout different production phases;
- Conducting quality assessments based on the established quality plan;
- Ensuring defective products do not proceed into the supply chain.

 - Work full-time in a rotating 5-shift pattern (06:00–14:00, 14:00–22:00, 22:00–06:00);
- Earn a competitive salary of €3,236 monthly, which includes a 28.5% shift bonus;
- Receive a travel reimbursement of €0.23 per kilometer, with no upper limit;
- Access various opportunities to grow personally and professionally within the organization;
- Start saving for your pension from day one under Covebo;
- Enjoy 25 vacation days provided through Covebo;
- Benefit from an 8.33% holiday bonus via Covebo;
- Explore the chance to secure a permanent role with Canpack after your time with Covebo.

 - Excellent command of English, both verbal and written;
- Hands-on experience with tools and methods for quality assurance;
- Exceptional analytical abilities and attention to detail;
- Familiarity with safety protocols and hygiene standards;
- Skilled in using Microsoft Office programs.

 For over 30 years, Canpack Helmond has been a leader in the metal packaging industry. With a strong presence in Central and Eastern Europe and expanding into Western Europe, Asia, and Africa, they are one of the largest manufacturers of metal packaging worldwide. Their dedicated team of nearly 8,000 employees produces approximately 25 billion beverage cans, 28 billion bottle closures, 1 billion metal containers for the food and chemical industries, and 700 tons of glass packaging annually.

Are you an experienced forklift operator who feels right at home in a logistics environment? Would you like to work for a stable company where you’ll work alongside a small, close-knit team to ensure everything runs smoothly? Then we have a great opportunity for you!

For a client in Weert, we’re looking for an experienced forklift operator who enjoys working the night shift. You’ll be joining a large logistics company where safety, teamwork, and a pleasant work environment are top priorities.

What will you be doing?

As a forklift operator, you’ll be responsible for moving goods efficiently and safely within the warehouse. You’ll spend most of your workday operating the forklift. Together with four colleagues, you’ll ensure that all pallets and goods are placed in the correct locations and that outbound orders are ready on time.

Your duties will include:

- Loading and unloading trucks;
- Picking orders and preparing them for shipment;
- Scanning goods;
- Moving pallets and goods within the warehouse;
- Preparing outgoing orders for transport.

You’ll be operating a forklift with double forks, loading from the side. Do you have experience with this? If so, be sure to read on!

You’ve already gained considerable experience operating a forklift and understand how important it is to work safely and accurately. You’re flexible, keep a cool head during busy periods, and are comfortable working two different shifts.

In addition:

- You have recent experience as a forklift operator;
- You hold a valid forklift operator’s certificate;
- You are fluent in Dutch or English;
- You are available full-time;
- You work with precision and always put safety first.
